     "id": "notes-1",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "- **Purpose.** See MRS $= w/p$ as a tangency: the best hours are where the highest reachable indifference curve just touches the budget line. Moving $w$ or $p$ shows that only the real wage moves hours ($h = w/(6p)$ in the example).\n- **Model.** A view of [Labor-Leisure Choice Model](note:labor-leisure-choice-model). Leisure is on the horizontal axis, so hours worked are read leftward from 24.\n- **Elements.** Panel `choice`: curves `budget`, `ic_opt`, `ic_probe` (dashed, through the trial point); points `optimum` and `probe` (draggable along the budget line, bound to `lp`). Readouts `h_out`, `l_out`, `c_out`, `mrs_out`, `hp_out`, `mrsp_out`."
      }
     ],
     "words": 97,
     "symbols": [
      "$h$",
      "$w$",
      "$p$",
      "$w/p$"
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "notes-2",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "- **Goal it supports.** `abs(lp - lstar) < 0.06`: with step 0.05 the slider meets it at 20.65 and 20.70.\n- **Tests.** Lecture example numbers and the goal's grid points, computed independently in Python."
      }
     ],
